{"_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": ""}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "Graphics Formats, BMP, EPS and GIF"}, {"type": "position", "content": 5}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 2}, {"type": "level", "content": "A2.2"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you hear/use when you talk about graphic formats."}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Learning Outcome"}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level.   Exchanges simple information on the design of an information system, computer architecture and hardware, and basic concepts on graphic design."}], "type": "objectives"}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "enpe8n4le02ob05re1img01.jpg"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Look for information about graphic formats."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Make a summary about the different graphic formats"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Make a comparative chart in a poster explaining the different graphic formats."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Share and explain your poster in class."}], "type": "takeaway_extension"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I search additional information about graphic formats."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I summarize information about graphic formats."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I create a poster explaining the differences among graphic formats."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I explain some general ideas about graphic formats in class"}], "type": "takeaway_assessment"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Order of Adjectives"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "When you are describing an object you can say many characteristics about it, those characteristics need to go in a specific order."}, {"type": "text", "content": "The order of the adjectives depends on the type of adjectives you use in the description. In the following chart you can see the order depending on the type of adjectives you are using:"}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":7,\"columns\":3,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Order\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Type\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Example\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"1\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Opinion\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"exceptional, nice, strange\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"2\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Size\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"big, small, huge, tall\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"3\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Physical quality\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"thin, fat, \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"4\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Shape\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"cylindrical, conical, square\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"5\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Age\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"old, young, senior\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"6\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Color\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"blue, green, black, red\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\"\"}"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Remember the adjectives always go before the noun you are talking about."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Example:</br>  <i>This is a <b>brand-new, cutting-edge, pricey</b> video card! </i></br> <i>This is an <b>advanced, flexible, well-developed</b> graphic format. </i></br>"}, {"type": "example", "content": "They are a self-contained, multimedia, portable and a bit outdated format which designers who need to have very powerful PCs and video cards use."}, {"type": "example", "content": "You can also save low-resolution, monochrome or full-color, static, light images."}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Common Time Expressions Used in Future Tenses"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "When using future tenses, time expressions can help you determine the approximate time when you think the action will happen. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "These are some of the most common expressions that you can use with future tenses:</br> </br> <u>Tomorrow</u></br> <i>I will send you the photo files tomorrow.</i> </br> </br> <u>In a year/month/week</u></br> <i>We will use a newer image format next week. </i></br> </br> <u>Soon</u></br> <i>They will develop a light image format with low compression soon. </i></br> <i>More technological tools will be available to them soon. </i></br> </br> <u>On Monday / Tuesday\u2026</u></br> </br> <i>We will review the different image files on Friday. </i></br> </br> <u>Later</u></br> <i>She'll send me the animated GIFs later. </i></br> </br> <u>Next month / week / year</u></br> <i>We'll participate in the digital photo conference next year. </i>"}, {"type": "example", "content": "I will save some of my pictures in the format you mentioned later."}, {"type": "example", "content": "I'll save the monochrome images I have in that format. I'll do that tomorrow."}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "low-quality "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "average, low-grade or low-caliber  "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I don't want them to be low-quality, but I don't want them to be too heavy either."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n4le02ob05aud01"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "pixel "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "the smallest unit in digital images, it represents a dot"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Basically, all formats specify the colors of every single pixel or dot that you can see in an image."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n4le02ob05aud02"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "compressed "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "something that is pressed to use less space"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Some are highly compressed to save space and others are very large."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n4le02ob05aud03"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "self-contained"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "something that makes a single unit or that is independent  "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: They're called encapsulated Postscripts. They are a self-contained, multimedia, portable and a bit outdated format."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n4le02ob05aud04"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "outdated"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "old-fashioned or not currently used "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: They're called encapsulated Postscripts. They are a self-contained, multimedia, portable and a bit outdated format. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n4le02ob05aud05"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "low-resolution "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "in computers and images, it refers to something with not much detail or lacking sharpness "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: You can also save low-resolution, monochrome or full-color, static, light images."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n4le02ob05aud06"}], "type": "target_word"}], "type": "sena", "labs": [{"stimuli": [{"template_override": 1, "_data": [], "id": 0, "type": "welcome", "contents": [{}]}, {"_data": [], "contents": [{"value": {"images": [{"time": "0", "image": "enpe8n4le02ob05re2img01.jpg", "id": 0, "text": "<p><strong>Sean: </strong>I can't decide which format to use to save these images. I don't want them to be low-quality, but I don't want them to be too heavy either. What should I do?</p>\n<p><strong>Tom: </strong>There are many graphic formats, but the final choice depends on what you plan to do with those images.</p>\n<p><strong>Sean:</strong> I know a little about BMPs, GIFs, and EPS, but I don't know which one to choose.</p>\n<p><strong>Tom: </strong>Basically, all formats specify the colors of every single pixel or dot that you can see in an image, they have different purposes depending on the user, some are highly compressed to save space and others are very large. Speaking of the formats you mentioned, BMPs or bit maps are very large, accurate and widely-used. The problem is that they use a lot of storage space.</p>"}, {"time": "49000", "image": "enpe8n4le02ob05re2img02.jpg", "id": 1, "text": "<p><strong>Sean: </strong>Well, I will save some of my pictures in the format you mentioned later, I want to preserve the quality as much as possible. But what about the photos I want to post online?</p>\n<p><strong>Tom: </strong>Well, in that case, EPS format won't be suitable for that either. They're called encapsulated Postscripts. They are a self-contained, multimedia, portable and a bit outdated format which designers who need to have very powerful PCs and video cards use.</p>\n<p><strong>Sean: </strong>So, that leaves GIFs, but you use it to show short animations, don&rsquo;t you?</p>"}, {"time": "83100", "image": "enpe8n4le02ob05re2img03.jpg", "id": 2, "text": "<p><strong>Tom: </strong>Not only that! You can also save low-resolution, monochrome or full-color, static, light images. GIFs are highly-compressed and they will hold only 256 colors. You commonly use them on websites because they don't need a lot of storage space.</p>\n<p><strong>Sean: </strong>I'll save the monochrome images I have in that format. I'll do that tomorrow. However, I don't know what to do with the full-color images, they'll surely look pixelated in that format.</p>"}], "audiosrc": "enpe8n4le02ob05re2aud01\t", "coverimg": "enpe8n4le02ob05re2img01.jpg"}, "type": "slideshow"}], "type": "audio", "template_override": 1, "id": 1, "title": ""}], "exercises": [{"stimuli_ids": [0], "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "I can give detailed information about graphic formats."}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "I can talk about BMP, EPS and GIF."}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "I can explain how BMP, EPS, and GIF are used."}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": "What do you know about graphic formats? What are their differences?"}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": "How can you prevent compression from affecting image quality? Explain."}], "type": "instructions"}, {"contents": [{"type": "group_name", "content": "Welcome"}], "type": "group"}, {"type": "feedback", "content": {"attempt_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "You have 2 tries"}, {"type": "text", "content": "you have 1 attempt left"}], "correct_feedback": "Correct", "incorrect_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "try again"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Maybe next time"}], "allowed_attempts": 2}}, {"type": "free_header_text", "content": "Ask your partner:"}, {"type": "free_type_text_area", "content": "There are too many formats!"}], "questions": [], "type": "WLC", "img_path": "", "id": 0, "template_override": 1}, {"stimuli_ids": [1], "_data": [{"c